Let me write it properly with the standard slab method which handles both directions.

```
let t_enter = 0, t_exit = Infinity;
let axis = null;

function slab(o, d, min, max) {
  let t1, t2;
  if (Math.abs(d) < EPS) {
    if (o < min || o > max) return null; // parallel outside
    return [0, Infinity];
  }
  t1 = (min - o) / d;
  t2 = (max - o) / d;
  if (t1 > t2) [t1, t2] = [t2, t1];
  return [t1, t2];
}
```

For axis resolution, track which axis produced the max t_enter. The face is the axis with the larger entry time (the one hit last / the limiting one).

Let me implement:

```js
function sweptEntry(bx0, by0, bx1, by1, o, x0, y0, x1, y1) {
  const dx = x1 - x0, dy = y1 - y0;
  let tEnter = 0, tExit = Infinity;
  let axis = null, axisEnter = 0;

  // X slab
  if (Math.abs(dx) < 1e-9) {
    if (x0 <= bx0 || x0 >= bx1) return null;
  } else {
    let a = (bx0 - x0) / dx, b = (bx1 - x0) / dx;
    if (a > b) { const t = a; a = b; b = t; }
    if (b < tEnter) return null;
    if (a > tEnter) { tEnter = a; axis = 'x'; axisEnter = a; }
    if (b < tExit) tExit = b;
  }
  // Y slab
  if (Math.abs(dy) < 1e-9) {
    if (y0 <= by0 || y0 >= by1) return null;
  } else {
    let a = (by0 - y0) / dy, b = (by1 - y0) / dy;
    if (a > b) { const t = a; a = b; b = t; }
    if (b < tEnter) return null;
    if (a > tEnter) { tEnter = a; axis = 'y'; axisEnter = a; }
    if (b < tExit) tExit = b;
  }

  if (tEnter > tExit || tEnter > 1) return null;
  // overlap already existing at t=0? handled: if entering (moving toward) it registers axis.
  if (axisEnter === 0) {
    // overlap at start — fall back to penetration-based face
    ...
  }
  return { t: tEnter, axis };
}
```

Hmm, the axis with the greater entry time is the limiting face (the face actually hit). This gives the correct outward normal:
- if axis 'x' and dx>0 → moving right → hit left face → flip vx. If dx<0 → hit right face → flip vx.
- Similarly axis 'y': dy<0 → hit top face → flip vy (since moving up). dy>0 → hit bottom → flip vy.

